949 0 obj
<<
/Title (For Italian cities, we find a strong and statistically significant positive relationship between Airbnb listings and residential rents.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 897 0 R
/Next 953 0 R
>>
endobj
950 0 obj
<<
/Title (It is important to emphasize that this result reflects correlation rather than strong causal identification.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 897 0 R
/Prev 954 0 R
>>
endobj
951 0 obj
<<
/Title (Our Mission)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 946 0 R
>>
endobj
952 0 obj
<<
/Title (Rents respond immediately to the supply shock)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 947 0 R
>>
endobj
953 0 obj
<<
/Title (In the main specification, a doubling of listings is associated with an increase of approximately 159 euros per month for a standard 70-square-meter apartment.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 897 0 R
/Prev 949 0 R
/Next 954 0 R
>>
endobj
954 0 obj
<<
/Title (However, this effect is not uniform across cities. It is strongest in Milan, weaker in Rome, and not statistically significant in Florence. This suggests that local market conditions play an important role.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 897 0 R
/Prev 953 0 R
/Next 950 0 R
>>
endobj
